The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (call->out_dir_scb != call->out_scb) {
    ret = xdr_decode_AFSFetchStatus(&bp, call, call->out_scb);
}
```
Reason:
This conditional check only decodes the second file status when the source and destination directories are different. If they are the same, the second status is not decoded, which prevents the xdr pointer from advancing correctly, leading to an incorrect reading of the volsync record.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = xdr_decode_AFSFetchStatus(&bp, call, call->out_scb);
ret = xdr_decode_AFSFetchStatus(&bp, call, call->out_scb);
```
Reason:
By always decoding the second status regardless of whether the source and destination directories are the same, the xdr pointer is correctly advanced, ensuring that the volsync record is read accurately. This allows the directory data version numbers to be reliably updated.

